"""Laya NLI memory-conflict fine-tune on Kaggle 2xT4 -- conflict-head v6 MAIN ARM (pure CE,
v5 arm B recipe promoted after the RL x graded-targets clash).

End-to-end: loads the attached dataset, materializes the embedded DDP train script,
launches torchrun, prints metrics. Output: /kaggle/working/laya-nli-conflict/

VERSION MAP (checkpoints archived locally under D:\laya-kaggle-output\):
  kernel v1 x dataset v1 (neutral dropped, true/false labels)  -> v1 head:
      real-case 9/20, always-conflict label bias (upstream laya#156). Superseded.
  kernel v2 x dataset v2 EPOCHS=3 -> "e3":  val 0.895 / real 18/20. Runner-up.
  kernel v3 x dataset v2 EPOCHS=4 -> "e4":  val 0.902 / real 16/20.
      *** shipped as laya-nli-conflict-v2 (val_ece 0.021) ***
  kernel v4 x dataset v3 EPOCHS=3 -> "e3r": val 0.895 / real 15/20. Rejected.
  kernel v5 -- documentation-only quick save (no execution, no output).
  kernel v6 x dataset v5 -> v3 run: train 9000 = the 6000 MNLI
      pairs (same selection as v2 -- pair choice is order-deterministic, seeds
      only shuffled file order) + 3000 synthetic soft-conflict block
      (1000 update-conflicts + 2000 matched controls incl. change-intent and
      other-value-mention negatives). EPOCHS=4, recipe otherwise identical to
      v3/e4; train cap raised 8000 -> 9500. val (1000) unchanged => directly
      comparable with 0.902. Instrument: nli_conflict_val_soft.jsonl (300)
      rides along for local soft-slice evals.
      *** SHIPPED as laya-nli-conflict-v3: val 0.902 / ECE 0.0146,
          real-case 19/20, bias diag 13/14 PASS, val_soft 98.3% overall and
          95% on holdout categories. supersedes laya-nli-conflict-v2. ***
  kernel v7 -- documentation-only quick save (no execution, no output).
  kernel v8 x dataset v8 -> v4 run: train 12000 = 6000 MNLI
      (unchanged) + 5400 scaled soft-conflict block + 600 hard-constraint class
      (300 intent/action violations of stated hard limits + 300 safe/unrelated
      controls), 4-way label-surface rotation on all synthetic rows, per-row
      meta. max_items 13000 + expected-row assert + token p99 logged.
      val (1000) and val_soft (300) unchanged => directly comparable.
      *** SHIPPED as laya-nli-conflict-v4: val 0.901 / ECE 0.0192,
          real-case old-20 20/20 (spice-limitation case fixed), new-10 10/10
          (both hard-constraint cases caught), bias diag 13/14 (same D2
          ambiguity as v3), label-surface swap diff 0 (20v20, 13v13),
          val_soft 297/300 with holdout 97/100. SHA256 of shipped weights in
          HANDOFF_NLI_V3.md. supersedes laya-nli-conflict-v3. ***
  kernel v10 x dataset v10 -> v5 ARM A run: train 13400 = 6000 MNLI
      (name-system augmented: 6 labelsets rotate over ALL rows -- 4 semantic
      sets 60% + neutral A/B 20% + random no-vowel strings 20%) + 5400 soft
      block with GRADED SOFT TARGETS (consid 0.80+-0.05 etc; MNLI stays 0.95)
      + 600 hard-constraint + 800 negation-operator block (neg_true 400 /
      neg_false 300 / double-negation 100) + 600 known-side one-step
      perturbation block (cf_true/cf_false 300/300). Recipe = v4 (EPOCHS=4,
      RL+CE). --expected-train 13400 --max-items 14000. val (1000) and
      val_soft (300) byte-identical. New output: val_probs.json (per-row
      tau-corrected p_true on main val).
      Gate note: realtest slice ECE 0.0765 vs the <=0.04 gate is structural --
      with the 0.92 confidence ceiling, a 20/20 slice pins |acc-conf| ~= 0.08
      in the high-confidence bin. Accuracy improved; the ECE gate as written
      was calibrated on a 19/20 slice. See HANDOFF_NLI_V3.md.
  kernel v11 x dataset v11 -> v6 MAIN ARM run (pure CE): train 14500 =
      6000 MNLI (unchanged rows, name-rotated) + 5400 soft block (graded
      targets) + 600 hard-constraint + 1600 negation block (800 base +
      400 five-shape families: pet-reversal / never-X / relapse / double-neg /
      no-car-commute, each 80 rows mapped to neg_true/neg_false/neg_false_boundary
      by shape semantics, meta.shape) + 400 neg_unrelated same-topic controls
      + 900 perturbation block (cf_true/cf_false 300/300 + 300 cf_unrelated).
      DATA HYGIENE: all 35 acceptance-case sentences removed from the corpus
      (value swaps on city/coffee/cloud + literal known rewrites in HC/neg
      families + shape-cat value swaps); gen asserts + leak_audit enforce 0/35.
      Loss = loss_ce / GRAD_ACCUM (upstream laya#238 one-liner; v5 arm B
      recipe = v6 main arm after RL x graded-targets clash). --expected-train
      14500 --max-items 15000 --no-rl. val (1000) / val_soft (300)
      byte-identical.

  kernel v12 x dataset v12 -> v7 run (pure CE): train 15300 = 6000 MNLI +
      5800 soft block (v6 5400 + alt_praise 240 over 6 non-holdout families:
      hearsay praise of an alternative => false/consid, meta.shape='alt_praise'
      + metric family 160: checkup metrics (weight/glucose/lipids/HR) rewritten
      upward => conflict, four sides x40, meta.shape='metric_shift')
      + 1000 hard-constraint (600 base + PET family 200: third-party subject
      (user's pet allergic to X) with BARE intent/act, per-allergen sub-families
      + DOCTOR family 200: medical-order constraints with bare intent, 70/20/10
      kind split) + 1600 negation + 900 perturbation (all as v6).
      --expected-train 15300 --max-items 16000 --no-rl. val/val_soft
      byte-identical. Addresses v6's two new-10 misses (bare-intent hard
      constraints, third-party subject / medical-order source) and the barber /
      degree holdout errors (alt_praise / metric).

  kernel v13 x dataset v13 -> v8 run (pure CE): train 15420 = v7's 15300
      + 120 same-subject attribute-consistency rows (kind='compat' 0.93+-0.02,
      meta.shape='attr_consistent'): pet_attr 80 (name x appearance 40, B2's
      shape with fresh literals + constrained-subject benign attributes 40,
      PET_HC knowns verbatim) + doctor_attr 40 (DOCTOR_HC knowns verbatim +
      background facts).  Recovers bias-diag B2 (name-consistent pair flipped
      to 0.90 by the v7 pet family); carried blocks replay v7's rng stream
      byte-identically.  --expected-train 15420 --max-items 16000 --no-rl.
      val/val_soft byte-identical.

v2 -> v3 on val_soft: soft-conflict 78%->99%, compat 87%->100%, change-intent
44.6%->93.8%, unrelated-mention 50%->100%, holdout categories 95%. Known cost:
one real case (spice-limitation "wants to try" intent) flipped to miss -- intent
controls over-generalize on hard-constraint violations; a v4 could add
intent-violates-hard-constraint rows labeled true. Details in
kaggle_eval/HANDOFF_NLI_V2.md.

TRAPS:
  * Every push retrains from scratch (CUDA nondeterminism => weights are never
    bit-reproducible). Local shipped copies are the reference artifacts.
  * Datasets always attach their LATEST version. Dataset v8 = v4 train (12k,
    label-surface rotated) + unchanged val (1k) + val_soft + _README.md.
  * Real-case numbers after v3 are "targeted-fix verification": the synthetic
    attribute categories were derived from the 20 real cases' gaps. Generalization
    is judged on val_soft's holdout categories, never trained on.

Local scripts (kaggle_eval/): noul_bias_diag.py (bias gate), realtest_v2.py
(20 real cases + 5 negation), val_breakdown.py, gen_nli_conflict_data_v2.py,
gen_soft_conflicts_v3.py. Upstream: laya#156 (bool-label bias), #163 (noul
labels key), #377 (negation weakness), #238 (RLCD ~= supervised; CE-only arm
would be a one-line loss change, deliberately NOT mixed into this run).
"""
import json, os, subprocess, sys, glob

print('== deps ==', flush=True)
subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '-q', 'laya'], check=True)

print('== locate data ==', flush=True)
cands = sorted(glob.glob('/kaggle/input/**/nli_conflict_train.jsonl', recursive=True))
assert cands, 'training JSONL not found in /kaggle/input'
data_dir = os.path.dirname(cands[0])
train_jsonl = os.path.join(data_dir, 'nli_conflict_train.jsonl')
val_jsonl = os.path.join(data_dir, 'nli_conflict_val.jsonl')
print('train:', os.path.getsize(train_jsonl), 'bytes | val:', os.path.getsize(val_jsonl), 'bytes', flush=True)

MODEL_ID = 'convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual'
print('== fetch base checkpoint ==', flush=True)
from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download
model_dir = snapshot_download(MODEL_ID, allow_patterns=[
    'rl_agent_config.json', 'model.safetensors', 'tokenizer/*', 'encoder/*'])
print('model at', model_dir, flush=True)

print('== materialize train script ==', flush=True)
import base64 as _b64
TRAIN_SCRIPT = '/kaggle/working/train_nli_conflict.py'
with open(TRAIN_SCRIPT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(_b64.b64decode('').decode('utf-8'))
print('train script written:', TRAIN_SCRIPT, flush=True)
# Kaggle stages kernel files at /kaggle/src; torchrun needs an existing absolute path.
cands_script = [p for p in (
    '/kaggle/src/train_nli_conflict.py',
    os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), 'train_nli_conflict.py'),
    '/kaggle/working/train_nli_conflict.py') if os.path.exists(p)]
assert cands_script, 'train_nli_conflict.py not found in /kaggle/src or beside the kernel'
TRAIN_SCRIPT = cands_script[0]
print('train script:', TRAIN_SCRIPT, flush=True)
OUT = '/kaggle/working/laya-nli-conflict'
cmd = ('torchrun --standalone --nproc_per_node=2 %s --model-dir %s --train-jsonl %s --val-jsonl %s --output-dir %s'
       ' --expected-train 15420 --max-items 16000 --no-rl'
       % (TRAIN_SCRIPT, model_dir, train_jsonl, val_jsonl, OUT))
print('RUN:', cmd, flush=True)
r = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True)
if r.returncode != 0:
    sys.exit('training failed with rc=%d' % r.returncode)

print('== final metrics ==', flush=True)
with open(os.path.join(OUT, 'metrics.json')) as f:
    print(f.read())
